course: dictionary
lesson: 13859
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: this is its context. «Juggling» is a good example.
explain: «Mia practises juggling three balls every morning.» Here juggling means throwing and catching objects so that at least one is always in the air. «Sam is juggling homework, football and piano this week.» Here juggling means trying to manage several things at the same time. The words around it give the clue.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence about balls, or about lots of jobs? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Juggling can mean throwing and catching several objects, like balls, so that at least one is always in the air.
fact: Juggling can also mean trying to do or manage several things at the same time.
fact: Juggling is a noun, and it is also the -ing form of the verb juggle: juggle, juggles, juggled, juggling.
fact: «Juggling» is often used with words like balls, clubs and scarves, as in juggling balls or juggling clubs.
fact: A juggling act can be a circus show, or a busy time when you have many things to manage.
exercise: «Mia practises juggling three balls every morning.» What does juggling mean here? | Sleeping late in bed | *Throwing and catching several balls so that one is always in the air | Reading a long book | Cooking dinner for the family
exercise: «Sam is juggling homework, football and piano this week.» What does juggling mean here? | Dropping all his things on the floor | *Trying to manage several things at the same time | Sitting still and resting | Throwing a ball very high
exercise: «Ava juggled three scarves at the school show.» Find and copy the verb form in this sentence. | scarves | *juggled | school | show
test: «The clown was juggling clubs in the middle of the circus ring.» What is juggling here? | Telling jokes to the crowd | Painting the clubs red | Carrying the clubs to the car | *Throwing and catching clubs so that at least one is always in the air
test: «Mrs Lee is juggling work and family, so she is always busy.» What does juggling suggest? | Sleeping in the afternoon | Playing with a ball in the garden | Dropping things on purpose | *Managing many things at once
exam: Which word is not a form of the verb juggle? | juggles | *juggler | juggled | juggling
